# Refactoring Rules

1. Refactoring preserves existing behavior. Do not fix bugs, alter UI strings, or add features.
2. Exactly one logical change per prompt. If other improvements are noticed, note them down; do not touch them.
3. Do not rename exported functions, component names, API endpoints, or prop contracts unless explicitly requested.
4. Do not install new third-party packages.
5. After every edit, run `npm test` and `npm run lint` in client/ and show the output.